nodecode-soniox is a rewrite of XimilalaXiang's XimilalaXiang/hermes-soniox:
https://github.com/XimilalaXiang/hermes-soniox
commit 79f8d1dec5fcdc75e22ec34e857e5b4e2b8828bf
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Xiang (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's two providers, its Soniox REST client and its
language and format helpers, as two Nodecode tools the model calls directly --
one that speaks text into an audio file, one that reads a recording back as
text -- with the same endpoints, request bodies and defaults (tts-rt-v2 with
Adrian and English, stt-async-v6 with language detection), the same 5000
character text limit, the same 0.7-to-1.3 speed clamp, the same format map
(ogg and opus both ask Soniox for opus), the same status polling with its
backoff and timeout, and the same best-effort deletion of the transcription
and the uploaded file afterwards. The key rides as an Authorization: Bearer
header and is redacted from every error the model reads, as the plugin did.
What was left out: the provider registration itself (Nodecode has no voice
provider slot), the manual page and config plumbing of the module, and the
realtime websockets the plugin did not implement either. The original's tests
were read for the behaviour, not translated.
